Name: quotedPrintableEncode

Type: function

Syntax: the quotedPrintableEncode of <data>

Syntax: quotedPrintableEncode(<data>)

Summary:
<return|Returns> a Quoted-Printable-<encode|encoded> string.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
put quotedPrintableEncode(messageBody) into emailBody

Parameters:
data (string):
A string of binary data of any length.

Returns:
The <quotedPrintableEncode> function <return|returns> a text <string>
representing the binary <data> in Quoted-Printable format.

Description:
Use the <quotedPrintableEncode> function to <encode> <binary file|binary
data> for use in MIME email bodies and headers, where most printable
ASCII characters are transmitted as-is and only non-printable or
non-ASCII bytes are escaped.

The <quotedPrintableEncode> function is the <inverse> of the
<quotedPrintableDecode> <function>. Printable ASCII characters (except
=) are passed through unchanged. All other bytes are encoded as =XX
where XX is the uppercase hexadecimal value of the byte. Lines are
wrapped at 76 characters using soft line breaks (=\r\n) as required by
RFC 2045.

For technical information about Quoted-Printable encoding, see
[RFC 2045, section 6.7](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045#section-6.7).

References: function (control structure), base64Encode (function),
quotedPrintableDecode (function), encode (glossary),
binary file (glossary), return (glossary), inverse (keyword),
string (keyword)

Tags: text processing
